==Trivia==
*The hog that he rides is most likely a "''Phacochoerus africanus''" ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_warthog common warthog]). Common Warthogs are smaller than boars but more agile which might explain why the Hog Rider can move particularly fast. Warthogs also have tusks, which is like the Hog Rider's hog in Clash Royale.
*The Hog Rider is 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Archer Queen]].
**The Hog Rider resembles the Level 1-2 Hog Rider from Clash of Clans.
*The Hog Rider is tied with [[Royal Hogs]], [[Princess]], [[Mother Witch|Cursed Hog]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Terry]] for the longest sight range of all troops, with a sight range of 9.5 tiles.
*The Hog Rider is one of the first troop [[cards]] to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Minions, Archers, [[Knight]], [[Spear Goblins]], Goblins, [[Bomber]], Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], Witch, P.E.K.K.A, [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The Hog Rider is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Royal Hogs, [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Hog Rider is 1 of 8 troops that can jump over the river, the others being Royal Hogs, [[Dark Prince]], Prince, [[Raging Prince]], Ram Rider, Cursed Hog, and Santa Hog Rider.
*In the French, German, Spanish, Dutch, Turkish, Arabic, Persian, Indonesian, and Malaysian language settings of the game, the Hog Rider's name translates to "Pig Rider". In the Italian, Thai, Finnish, Vietnamese and Portuguese language settings of the game, the Hog Rider's name translates to "Wild Boar Tamer", "Wild Boar Rider", "Hog Knight" and "Runner" respectively.
*The Hog Rider bears more than a passing resemblance to [[wikipedia:Mr._T|Mr. T]] and [https://streetfighter.fandom.com/wiki/Zangief Zangief] from Street Fighter.
*His description is based on the Clash of Clans [https://youtu.be/XH3Xu1-cvII Ride of the Hog Riders commercial].
**From his description, it is implied that the [[Arenas|Arena]] has doors leading to it.
*When the Hog Rider is deployed, he will occasionally yell "''Hog Riderrrrr!''"
**The Hog Rider is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being Mini P.E.K.K.A., [[Mega Minion]], Wizard, P.E.K.K.A., Dark Prince, Bowler, Ram Rider, [[Electro Wizard]], Princess, Ice Wizard, Magic Archer, [[Lumberjack]], Mother Witch, Fisherman, [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], Santa Hog Rider, [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], Archer Queen, [[Little Prince]], and the Terry.
*In Hog Mountain, 2 Hog Rider statues can be seen behind the enemy's [[King's Tower]].
*The [[Ranked|Master 2 League]] badge resembles a Hog Rider's hammer.
*According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=RamRiderComic.jpg strip], the Ram Rider is the Hog Rider's sister.
*The Hog Rider is featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Hog Rider is featured as [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Carl?file=Carl_Skin-Hog_Rider.png a character skin for Carl] in Brawl Stars.
**The Hog Rider, along with the Goblins, Barbarians, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, and the Archer Queen, were featured as a non-playable opponent in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess].
**The Hog Rider, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, Musketeer, Wizard, [[Battle Healer]], Witch, Miner, Ice Wizard, and Bandit, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squaddies Squaddie] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
***Along with the Goblin, Barbarian, Wizard, and Witch, he has the same rarity in both games.
*The Hog Rider, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Witch, Prince, and Night Witch, is featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater].
*The Hog Rider is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Hog Rider is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Hog Rider is the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
***It is also 1 of 3 cards in which an Emote he is the subject of relates to one of its [[Star Points|Star Levels]], the others being the [[Elite Barbarians]] and [[Rocket]].
**The Hog Rider is the subject of a Tower Skin.
**The Hog Rider is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Riders decoration is created by Myoho.
***The Snow Leopard decoration is part of a collaboration with [https://www.playing4theplanet.org/participants/clash-royale Green Game Jam 2023].
***The Hog Hammers frame's description says "''Yes, we know what time it is. No, we are not going to say it.''", which is a reference to the hip hop song "[https://youtu.be/otCpCn0l4Wo?si=m8_Da_vJq2Jua_S5 U Can't Touch This]" by the MC Hammer.
***The Hogley Davriderson decoration is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harley-Davidson Harley-Davidson], a motorcycle manufacturer.
*The Hog Rider was featured in the winning decks of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Hog Rider was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VxEzjdKQ4HA Clash Royale Helsinki Tournament], by a player called Jason.
**The Hog Rider was featured in the winning deck of the [https://youtu.be/LWQjS0e6iiE Super Magical Cup Tournament], by a player called CMcHugh.
**The Hog Rider was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/C5qBcdcErfM?si=e37mhAgNKAA5kMJI Clash Royale League 2018 Tournament], by a player called Lciop.
*In the [https://youtu.be/iXOgPaHXxWo?si=Dp2YCKpiE35sCRUo Quests intro video], there was a [[Quests|Quest]] that required the player to hit [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]] with a Hog Rider 10 times. However, this Quest never made it to the game.
*His Star Level 3 skin is not the same as it is shown in the [https://youtu.be/FBRWUwm0_gY Star Levels commercial] and the [https://youtu.be/s67c93v1njk Star Level intro video]. In the commercial and the intro video, he has a fully golden beard mustache and mohawk, whereas in-game only his mohawk is golden.
*Despite the Damage Dealer [[Card Mastery]] task mentioning that the Hog Rider can deal damage to troops or [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]], he cannot progress the task by dealing damage to troops.
**The Hog Rider is 1 of 6 troops that cannot deal damage to other troops whatsoever, the others being the [[Royal Giant]], Giant, Royal Hogs, Elixir Golem, and [[Rune Giant]].
*Before the Hog Rider's card release, the Hog Rider's damage was decreased by 5%.

